      "claim": "Encainide absolute oral bioavailability in normal subjects was 32±7%, above the 20% threshold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C40"],
      "claim": "In 20 normal young men, verapamil bioavailability averaged 19.4% after oral doses, just below the 20% threshold.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a lipophilic dimethoxy-substituted amine/lactam resembling verapamil, noscapine, and encainide. All close analogues have measured oral bioavailability mostly 22-42%, above the 20% threshold, with only borderline verapamil values near 19-20%. Therefore high (F>=20%) is better supported.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "Verapamil, the closest analogue, has values straddling the threshold (18-20%, 19.4%), creating borderline uncertainty.",
    "No data on first-pass metabolism or transporter effects specific to the query's lactam/tetrahydroisoquinoline scaffold."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
